<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf al-Fihri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 759</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Yusuf ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Fihri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf al-Fihri was governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> from 747 to 756, a member of the Fihrid family descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a>. He ruled largely independently as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> collapsed. In 756 he was defeated by the Umayyad prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-i">Abd al-Rahman I</a>, who made himself emir at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, and he was killed in 759 after a failed revolt.</p></div>
